• Can the product be disassembled and reassembled by a technician without specialist training?
• What is the minimum number of distinct parts needed to maintain product functionality?
• Are all fasteners and connection points visible and accessible without removing unrelated components?
• Can the reassembly sequence be completed correctly without reference to detailed instructions?
• Does the product design avoid any "traps" — hidden fasteners, non-obvious snap-fits, or components that appear removable but are permanently attached?